ings/call-transcripts/2026/04/29/formfactor-form-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"FORM 2026 Q3","e":"form","d":"2026-10-28","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Aric McKinnis","x":"Our position at the intersection of high-performance compute and advanced packaging provides broad exposure across the AI compute architecture from HBM paired with advanced GPUs, CPUs and custom ASICs to emerging co-packaged optics and other photonics applications.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/formfactor-form-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"FORM 2026 Q3","e":"form","d":"2026-10-28","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Aric McKinnis","x":"Approximately $10.5 million or about 380 basis points, of benefit resulted primarily from tariff refunds and favorable subcomponent costs in our Quantum business that are not expected to recur.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/formfactor-form-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"FORM 2026 Q3","e":"form","d":"2026-10-28","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Aric McKinnis","x":"The favorable impact of tariff refunds on gross margins in the third quarter was about 300 basis points, or $8.6 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/formfactor-form-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"FORM 2026 Q3","e":"form","d":"2026-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mike Slessor","x":"This mix shift was also expected with HBM revenue declining and DDR5 revenue increasing as our customers move their wafer start mix to more DDR designs to capture the profit opportunity provided by significant DDR market price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/formfactor-form-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"FORM 2026 Q3","e":"form","d":"2026-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mike Slessor","x":"If I look at the DRAM gross margins and parse them, there's very little contribution from price i